  "id": "COMPOUND:22485 - PROTEIN:6154",
  "verbalization": "Javanicoside F appears to have a direct relationship with Prelamin-A/C through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Javanicoside F targets Ataxin-2, which is a target of Diplotrin A, and Diplotrin A in turn targets Prelamin-A/C. This pathway implies that Javanicoside F may exert its effects by modulating the activity of Diplotrin A, which is involved in the regulation of Prelamin-A/C. Additionally, Javanicoside F is also shown to target another subunit of the 26S proteasome, which is a target of Diplotrin A, further reinforcing the link between Javanicoside F and Prelamin-A/C through a potentially distinct mechanism.\n\nThe integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Javanicoside F in influencing the proteasomal degradation of Prelamin-A/C, possibly through the modulation of Diplotrin A. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of Diplotrin A suggest that Javanicoside F may act as a modulator of the proteasome pathway, which is a well-established mechanism in cellular homeostasis. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Javanicoside F and Prelamin-A/C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The findings align with the expectation of a biologically relevant mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the therapeutic implications.",
